course: dictionary
lesson: 8311
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The words around it, its context, show you which meaning is right. «We had a roast dinner on Sunday.» Dinner and Sunday are the clues, so roast means food cooked in an oven or over a fire.
explain: «Mum put the potatoes in the oven to roast.» Oven and potatoes tell you that roast means to cook food with dry heat. Check by putting your meaning into the sentence: "to cook" fits, so you are right.
explain: «Ellie started to roast her brother after he lost the match, and everyone laughed.» Roast does not mean cooking here. The laughing and the teasing tell you it means to make fun of someone sharply. «I'm roasting in this coat!» is a third meaning: very hot.
fact: «Roast» means to cook food, like meat or vegetables, in an oven or over a fire.
fact: «Roast potatoes» are potatoes cooked this way, and a «Sunday roast» is a big meal of roasted meat with vegetables.
fact: In young slang, «roast» means to make fun of someone sharply, and informally «I'm roasting!» means I'm very hot.
fact: Around a campfire, people roast marshmallows, holding them over the flames until they are golden.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Mum put the potatoes in the oven to roast.» What does roast mean here? | To wash food in cold water | To eat food very quickly | To freeze food until it is hard | *To cook food in an oven or over a fire
exercise: «We had a Sunday roast with all the trimmings.» What is a Sunday roast? | A long walk in the park | *A big meal with roasted meat | A kind of bread | A card game played on Sundays
exercise: «It's so hot in here, I'm roasting!» What does roasting mean? | Covered in mud | *Very hot | Angry with a friend | Cooking dinner
test: «Dandelion roots were roasted and used to make a drink like coffee.» What could people make from roasted dandelion roots? | A pair of socks | A kite | A cake | *A drink like coffee
test: «Dad roasted marshmallows over the campfire.» What does roasted mean here? | Thrown into water | Eaten all at once | *Cooked over the heat of a fire | Painted bright colours
exam: «Ellie said her brother looked like a clown in that hat, and everyone laughed. She really roasted him.» What does roasted mean here? | To hit him with a ball | To dry him with a towel | *To make fun of him sharply | To cook him in an oven
